@crew torres-zeke
// Head writer 4: career lines. Torres walked you up from the Tern; he trained you. He takes it personally, kindly.
== career.worried
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.missed
- Your board slot was empty this morning. Coil three noticed. So did I. You all right?
? tier>=colleague flag:career.low
- Calder's called you in? Go early. Say it straight. She respects straight.
? tier>=friend flag:career.verylow
- Up top to the Captain. {sigh}. I trained you, shipmate. I know what you can do.   #serious
? tier>=friend flag:career.bottom
- I'll knock at ten to eight. Not eight. Ten to. We walk down together.   #serious
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.up
- That's my trainee. Board, job, turn in. Like I showed you.
== career.eve
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.eve
- Tomorrow, then. I'll be at the Tern. Same spot as when you came.   #warm
? tier>=friend flag:career.eve
- I keep going over it. What I'd have said. Doesn't matter now. I'm sorry, shipmate.   #serious
== career.bye
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.lastday
- Today, then. I'll walk you down. Least I can do.   #warm
== career.seeoff
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.lastday
- Window seat. Every time. You remember.   #warm
== career.leave
? flag:leave.booked
- Leave tomorrow? Good. Don't come near the bay. I mean it.
== career.back
? flag:leave.back
- Back! Coil three behaved while you were off. Suspicious, honestly.   #funny
